 "deviations": [
  "PD1. jpp_lens's stages run as the library functions of scripts/jpp_cli.py (loaded by path), not through its command line, and with a stand-in module named pandas (pandas is not installed; no download beyond the three approved sources is approved): any attribute raises when looked up, except DataFrame and Series, which jpp_lens's signatures name at import and which raise when built. No stage used it. Not run: grade_model_correctness and the correctness CSV (they need pandas); R3 grades correctness itself (D8) with jpp_lens's own next_token_matches_target on the greedy token, so its grading is jpp_lens's by construction, not by test.",
  "PD2. The tiny run's sizes differ from the registered ones where a 32-wide model forces it or to keep it to seconds: PCA 16 (64 registered), 96 router records (1,000), 32 fit prompts (64) in 4 shards (8), 48 tokens (128), 8 rows per pass, a character tokenizer, made-up items in J++'s format. E = 8, skip 16, min kept 50, the R-lens rules, the split rule and the condense defaults are the registered ones.",
  "PD3. The weights are fitted by jpp_lens's own ExpertWeightingFitter, imported, not reimplemented, so the weight parity tests R3's inputs to it (fp16 experts, residuals, candidates, exclusions, the split).",
  "Matched, not deviations (the parity decides, R3_PREREG \u00a72): (a) the experts are rounded to fp16 before the weights are fitted and combined, because jpp_lens's fit-weights stage reads the fp16 experts file; the pooled R-lens comes from the in-memory fp32 sums (merge-experts --pooled-lens-out); (b) the weight surrogate sees softcapped logits (HFLensModel.unembed applies final_logit_softcapping); (c) the final norm is patched, as jpp_lens patches it; it is off the path of the block-output target (R3_lrp --selftest); (d) the exclusion list spares every candidate id of the six evals' items (readout_eval_items.py:191-212); (e) BOS is forced on raw text (HFLensModel force_bos): without it this tokenizer adds no BOS.",
  "Measured, a registered deviation (D4): R3's PCA is a streamed fp64 covariance where jpp_lens's fit_pca is fp32 on stored points; the router check above gives its size on the tiny run."
 ],
 "torch": "2.14.1+cu130"
}
